        "original_id": "66945835-9c70-5481-98a8-3ce72b0a1a95",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Jay Gould, Ann Beattie, Elisabeth Vrba\n- Concepts: Turnover Pulse Hypothesis, exaptation\n- Roles: popular science writer, novelist, short story writer, paleoanthropologist\n\nFacts:\n- Ann Beattie was born on September 8, 1947, and she is an American novelist and short story writer.\n- Stephen Jay Gould was one of the most influential and widely read popular science writers of his generation.\n- Elisabeth Vrba developed the Turnover Pulse Hypothesis.\n- Elisabeth Vrba coined the word exaptation with colleague Stephen Jay Gould.\n- The Turnover Pulse Hypothesis was constructed by paleoanthropologist Elisabeth Vrba.\n- The Turnover Pulse Hypothesis is used to gauge the rate of survival and adaptation within species.",
